5 177","corresponding":null,"first":"Saltanat","key":"nurmagambetovasaltanatpau","last":"Nurmagambetova","name":"Nurmagambetova, Saltanat","rank":211,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"178","corresponding":null,"first":"Yasser Abu","key":"jameiyasserabupau","last":"Jamei","name":"Jamei, Yasser Abu","rank":212,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"179 180","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"weisermarkpau","last":"Weiser","name":"Weiser, Mark","rank":213,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"99 4 95 100 101","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph U","key":"correllchristophupau","last":"Correll","name":"Correll, Christoph U","rank":214,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39341043"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.euroneuro.2024.07.010","issn":["0924977X","18737862"],"issn_org":["0924977X"],"journal":"European Neuropsychopharmacology","pages":"1-15","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Neuropsychopharmacology","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205003992"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-55072dc6-7789-4b7f-af92-5d91e2514894","sdu-476f88d8-db9c-42f7-8f6a-c031fe117421"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Collaborative outcomes study on health and functioning during infection times (COH-FIT) : Insights on modifiable and non-modifiable risk and protective factors for wellbeing and mental health during the COVID-19 pandemic from multivariable and network analyses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-814029","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Summary: Osteoporosis significantly impacts healthcare costs in Denmark, with annual expenses exceeding €3097 per individual. The total annual burden of healthcare and productivity losses attributed to osteoporosis in Denmark surpasses €2 billion. Effective prevention, early detection, and management strategies should be considered to offset these costs and improve patient outcomes. Purpose: As the prevalence of osteoporosis rises, driven by an ageing population, quantifying its financial impact and guiding resource allocation becomes crucial. The aim of this paper is to establish the healthcare (medical and social care) costs and productivity costs attributable to osteoporosis and osteoporosis-related fractures in Denmark. Methods: The osteoporosis and osteoporosis fracture groups were identified from Danish healthcare registers using ICD-10 codes. The intervention group included individuals born in 1930–1950 with an osteoporosis diagnosis or an osteoporotic fracture with incidence between 2000 and 2021. A control group without osteoporosis and osteoporosis fractures was matched 1: 1 on a number of clinical and demographic variables from the general Danish population. Difference-in-difference approach was applied through generalised estimating equations with individual-level fixed effects to establish attributable costs. Results: Osteoporosis and osteoporosis-related fractures can be attributed with more than €3097 annually in healthcare costs for individuals aged 50 to 91, with expenses increasing sharply with age. Cumulative attributable healthcare (medical and social care) cost of osteoporosis between the ages of 50 and 91 was estimated at reach €127,000 per person. For the identified population of over 667,000 people with osteoporosis, the total annual healthcare burden attributable to the disease would amount to over €2 billion. The osteoporosis group also incurred an annual productivity loss of €3883, until the age of 66. Conclusion: Osteoporosis carries a pronounced economic burden for the health system and the individual. Resource allocative decisions should consider whether implementing strategies improving prevention, earlier detection, and better management of osteoporosis could be efficient given the high identified costs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sopina, Liza","Hitz, Mette Friberg","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Langdahl, Bente Lomholt","Ladefoged, Benedicte Torp","Kruse, Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807670"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sopina, Liza"],"keyword":["Danish registers","Osteoporosis","Register based study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"healthcare and productivity cost of osteoporosis a danish register based quasi experimental study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00198-025-07453-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-807670","identifier":[{"id":"40111480","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105000483394","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-df0954a9-b3ac-41be-a2b6-948e1feb0b18"],"keyword":["Danish registers","Healthcare and productivity cost","Osteoporosis","Register based study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B9DBDAB12BF2FEB0E70FC06B0DF5E675"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00198-025-07453-w","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liza","key":"sopinapau","last":"Sopina","name":"Sopina, Liza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Friberg","key":"hitzpau","last":"Hitz","name":"Hitz, Mette Friberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lau Caspar","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","name":"Thygesen, Lau Caspar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"langdahlpau","last":"Langdahl","locid":"1c4e9957-996d-4c56-aa0d-4e57e7be12a5","name":"Langdahl, Bente Lomholt","name_org":"Langdahl, Bente","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedicte Torp","key":"ladefogedpau","last":"Ladefoged","name":"Ladefoged, Benedicte Torp","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"krusepau","last":"Kruse","name":"Kruse, Marie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40111480"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00198-025-07453-w","issn":["0937941X","14332965"],"issn_org":["0937941X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Osteoporosis International","pages":"865-874","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Osteoporosis International","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000483394"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-df0954a9-b3ac-41be-a2b6-948e1feb0b18"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Healthcare and productivity cost of osteoporosis : a Danish register-based quasi-experimental study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-807670","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background Multiple environmental and genetic factors play a role in the pathogenesis of atopic eczema (AE). We aimed to investigate gene–environment interactions (G × E) to improve understanding of the pathophysiology. Methods We analysed data from 16 European studies to test for interaction between the 24 most significant AE-associated loci identified from genome-wide association studies and 18 early-life environmental factors. We tested for replication using a further 10 studies and in vitro modeling to independently assess findings. Results The discovery analysis (including 25,339 individuals) showed suggestive evidence for interaction (p < 0.05) between seven environmental factors (antibiotic use, cat ownership, dog ownership, breastfeeding, elder sibling, smoking and washing practices) and at least one established variant for AE, 14 interactions in total. In the replication analysis (254,532 individuals) dog exposure × rs10214237 (on chromosome 5p13.2 near IL7R) was nominally significant (ORinteraction = 0.91 [0.83–0.99] p = 0.025), with a risk effect of the T allele observed only in those not exposed to dogs. A similar interaction with rs10214237 was observed for siblings in the discovery analysis (ORinteraction = 0.84 [0.75–0.94] p = 0.003), but replication analysis was under-powered (ORinteraction = 1.09 [0.82–1.46]). rs10214237 homozygous risk genotype is associated with lower IL-7R expression in human keratinocytes, and dog exposure modelled in vitro showed a differential response according to rs10214237 genotype. Conclusion Interaction analysis and functional assessment provide preliminary evidence that early-life dog exposure may modify the genetic effect of rs10214237 on AE via IL7R, supporting observational epidemiology showing a protective effect for dog ownership. The lack of evidence for other G × E studied here implies only weak effects are likely to occur.","author_count":76,"contributors":["Standl, Marie","Budu-Aggrey, Ashley","Johnston, Luke J.","Elias, Martina S.","Arshad, S. Hasan","Bager, Peter","Bataille, Veronique","Blakeway, Helena","Bønnelykke, Klaus","Boomsma, Dorret","Brumpton, Ben M.","Bustamante Pineda, Mariona","Campbell, Archie","Curtin, John A.","Eliasen, Anders","Fadista, João P.S.","Feenstra, Bjarke","Gerner, Trine","Medina-Gomez, Carolina","Grosche, Sarah","Gutzkow, Kristine B.","Halling, Anne-Sofie","Hayward, Caroline","Henderson, John","Herrera-Luis, Esther","Holloway, John W.","Hottenga, Joukejan","O’B Hourihane, Jonathan","Hu, Chen","Hveem, Kristian","Irizar, Amaia","Jacquemi, Benedicte","Jessen, Leon","Kress, Sara","Kurukulaaratchy, Ramesh J.","Lau, Susanne","Llop, Sabrina","Løset, Mari","Marenholz, Ingo","Mason, Dan","McCartney, Daniel L.","Melbye, Mads","Melén, Erik","Minica, Camelia","Murray, Clare S.","Nijsten, Tamar","Pardo, Luba M.","Pasmans, Suzanne","Pennell, Craig E","Rinnov, Maria Rasmussen","Santorelli, Gillian","Schikowski, Tamara","Sheehan, Darina","Simpson, Angela","Söderhall, Cilla","Thomas, Laurent F.","Thyssen, Jacob Pontoppidan","Torrent, Maties","van Beijsterveldt, Toos","Visconti, Alessia","Vonk, Judith M.","Wang, Carol A","Xu, Cheng-Jian","Ziyab, Ali H.","Custovic, Adnan","Di Meglio, Paola","Duijts, Liesbeth","Flohr, Carsten","Irvine, Alan D.","Koppelmann, Gerard H.","Lee, Young-Ae","Reynolds, Nick J","Smith, Catherine H.","Langan, Sinéad M.","Paternoster, Lavinia","Brown, Sara J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829663"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","France","Germany","Ireland","Italy","Kuwait","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Asthma and Allergy Research Centre","Barcelona Institute for Global Health","Biogipuzkoa HRI","Bradford Teaching Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Children’s Health Ireland","Cork University Hospital","Erasmus University Rotterdam","FISABIO–Universitat Jaume I–Universitat de València","German Center for Child and Adolescent Health (DZKJ)","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Hannover Medical School","Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Hunter Medical Research Institute","Ib Salut, Atencio Primaria de Menorca, Area Salut Menorca","Imperial College London","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","Johns Hopkins University","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","King Edward Memorial Hospital for Women","King's College London","Kuwait University","Leibniz Research Institute for Environmental Medicine","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust","Max Delbrück Center for Molecular Medicine in the Helmholtz Association","NHS Lothian","NIHR Southampton Biomedical Research Centre","Newcastle upon Tyne Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Norwegian Institute of Public Health","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Pompeu Fabra University","Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland","St John's Institute of Dermatology","St. Olav's University Hospital","St. Thomas' Hospital","Stanford University","Trinity College Dublin","UPV/EHU","University College Cork","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust","University Medical Center Groeningen","University of Bristol","University of Edinburgh","University of Groningen","University of Manchester","University of Newcastle","University of Southampton","University of Turin","University of Western Australia","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","École des hautes études en santé publique"],"keyword":["Atopic eczema","Dog","Environment","GENE","Interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3"