"key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Young-Ae","rank":71,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"43 53","first":"Nick J","key":"reynoldspau","last":"Reynolds","name":"Reynolds, Nick J","rank":72,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 54","first":"Catherine H.","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Catherine H.","rank":73,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"49 54 55","first":"Sinéad M.","key":"langanpau","last":"Langan","name":"Langan, Sinéad M.","rank":74,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 56","first":"Lavinia","key":"paternosterpau","last":"Paternoster","name":"Paternoster, Lavinia","rank":75,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 57","first":"Sara J","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, Sara J","rank":76,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40462597"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/all.16605","issn":["01054538","13989995"],"issn_org":["01054538"],"issue":"8","journal":"Allergy","pages":"2201-2212","status":"p","title":"Allergy","title_org":"Allergy: European Journal of Allergy and Clinical Immunology","volume":"80"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007759291"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b09ac321-c1c1-4396-9f3a-d7908122d638"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gene–Environment Interaction Affects Risk of Atopic Eczema : Population and In Vitro Studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829663","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To develop a clinician-guided, research-based guideline for adult outpatient psychotherapy for complex presentations of post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD). METHODS: We used state-of-the-art methods to develop clinical guideline recommendations and conduct systematic reviews with meta-analyses for five research questions: (Q1) When treating adults with PTSD, should trauma-focused psychotherapy include exposure? Which psychotherapies are effective for PTSD with co-occurring: (Q2) personality disorder; (Q3) depression; and (Q4) dissociative disorder? (Q5) for complex PTSD (C-PTSD)? RESULTS: (Q1) We found no evidence of a difference between trauma-focused psychotherapies with or without exposure on PTSD symptoms (standardised mean difference (SMD) 0.02, 95% CI -0.11 to 0.15, p=0.75, I2=64%). (Q2) Dialectical behaviour therapy (DBT-for-PTSD) showed beneficial effects over cognitive processing therapy (CPT) on co-occurring borderline personality disorder (BPD) symptoms (mean difference (MD) -0.58, 95% CI -0.94 to -0.22, p=0.003). (Q3) Mindfulness and body-focused psychotherapies, prolonged exposure (PE), narrative exposure therapy (NET) and CPT showed beneficial effects on symptoms of PTSD and co-occurring depression. Results for present-centred therapy (PCT) were uncertain. (Q4) No statistically significant differences were found among psychotherapies for PTSD with co-occurring dissociation. (Q5) Skills training appeared promising for C-PTSD. CONCLUSION: Weak clinical recommendations were reached for trauma-focused therapies with or without exposure for PTSD; DBT-for-PTSD for PTSD with co-occurring BPD; CPT, NET, PE and Mindfulness and body-focused psychotherapies for PTSD with co-occurring depression; and Skills training for C-PTSD. A weak recommendation was reached against PCT for PTSD with co-occurring depression. It is good practice to include interventions targeting dissociation for PTSD with co-occurring dissociation. Overall, the certainty of evidence was low; high-quality trials are needed to strengthen the recommendations. PROSPERO REGISTRATION NUMBER: CRD42022376117.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Schaug, Julie Perrine","Møller, Lise","Reinholt, Nina","Illum, Dyveke Bové","Græbe, Frida Lau","Mikkelsen, Line Bang","Austin, Stephen F.","Paulsen, Nina Nørrelykke","Porsing, Adrian Maria Tremel","Juul, Sophie","Hovmand, Oliver Rumle","Jørgensen, Mie Sedoc","Arendt, Ida Marie Terese Pereira","Quistgaard, Maria","Kristensen, Magnus Tang","Døssing, Sidsel Christine Buskbjerg","Rosenbaum, Bent","Rosenberg, Nicole Gremaud","Arnfred, Sidse","Storebø, Ole Jakob"],"cuid":["S02-089.24-804595"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Storebø, Ole Jakob"],"keyword":["Adult","Adult psychiatry","Anxiety disorders","Borderline Personality Disorder therapy","Depression mood disorders","Humans","Personality disorders","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Psychiatry","Psychotherapy methods","Stress Disorders Post Traumatic therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"psychotherapies for adults with complex presentations of ptsd a clinical guideline and five systematic reviews with meta analyses","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjment-2024-301158","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.24-804595","identifier":[{"id":"40234083","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003442526","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12004466","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-ff6bcab6-8853-41f7-8868-7d0f6aade1e9","sdu-fb14463f-3298-43