Franz","rank":112,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"enzingerchristianpau","last":"Enzinger","name":"Enzinger, Christian","rank":113,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David J","key":"werringdavidjpau","last":"Werring","name":"Werring, David J","rank":114,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"gattringerthomaspau","last":"Gattringer","name":"Gattringer, Thomas","rank":115,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39405058"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.39571","issn":["25743805"],"issue":"10","journal":"JAMA network open","paperid":"e2439571","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA network open","title_org":"JAMA Network Open","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206276935"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1be2f210-65f2-4502-9e2b-6d3edd26e17e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sex Differences in Frequency, Severity, and Distribution of Cerebral Microbleeds","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-769883","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: It is well-documented that people with inflammatory arthritis (IA) exhibit a high prevalence of symptoms related to anxiety and depression. Less is known about what contributes to good mental health in people with IA. Therefore, this study aims to explore how some patients maintain good mental health despite living with IA. METHODS: Explorative qualitative interview study (one focus group, 12 individual interviews, n = 18) utilizing purposeful sampling. All interviews were audiotaped, transcribed, and managed using NVivo14 and employed a reflexive thematical analysis approach. RESULTS: We identified four main themes: 1) Assisted by a positive outlook on life-how participants' inherent positivity helped them cope with arthritis; 2) Moving towards acceptance of life with arthritis-how participants embraced the reality of living with IA; 3) Counteracting letting arthritis dictate one's life how the participants structured their lives in terms of physical activity and social connections; and 4) Taking responsibility for the trajectory-how the participants were mindful of their bodies and took the initiative to explore new treatments. CONCLUSION: People living with IA maintain good mental health by engaging in structured physical activity, fostering social connections, and cultivating a positive outlook on life. These insights can inform the development of future treatment and support strategies.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Abild, Signe Marie","Midtgaard, Julie","Nordkamp, Annika","de Thurah, Annette","Vestergaard, Sofie Bech","Glintborg, Bente","Aadahl, Mette","Cromhout, Pernille Fevejle","Lau, Lene","Yilmaz, Connie","Esbensen, Bente Appel"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-767277"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Chronic illness","Disease Management","Inflammatory arthritis","Mental health","Qualitative studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Patient research partners"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"maintaining good mental health in people with inflammatory arthritis a qualitative study of patients perspectives","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17482631.2024.2424015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-767277","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11544728","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85208688835","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39506913","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1c9878d9-67ec-4d6b-8f01-d85c96ae40d1","ku-7b0bdcca-b4c4-42db-9297-52ae72bb3e5f"],"keyword":["Mental health","chronic illness","disease management","inflammatory arthritis","qualitative studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B1DEB8BBF25671EC8076B7FBE70C11B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17482631.2024.2424015","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/412385239/Maintaining_good_mental_health_in_people_with_inflammatory_arthritis_a_qualitative_study_of_patients_perspectives.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l