:"Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","first":"Selina Kikkenborg","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"92d15fb6-c29f-4d38-88a4-53d28ecc9a13","name":"Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37566892"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/inf.0000000000004063","issn":["08913668","10733175"],"issn_org":["08913668"],"issue":"11","journal":"Pediatric Infectious Disease Journal","pages":"999-1001","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Pediatric Infectious Disease Journal","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175194859"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-97630e0d-996d-4c14-a8e8-e83d9fcf8d03","sdu-2fc93dfe-4342-4aae-8bee-2016bde049a1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Risk of New-onset Type 1 Diabetes in Danish Children and Adolescents after SARS-CoV-2 Infection : A Nationwide, Matched Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.97-716465","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Stress is a widespread phenomenon and young people especially are experiencing high levels of stress. School-related factors are the most frequently self-reported stressors among adolescents, but few interventions have targeted the school environment. This study evaluated the effectiveness of the Healthy High School (HHS) intervention on stress at a 9-month follow-up. The study included 5201 first-year high school students (~16 years) in Denmark. Participating schools were randomized into the HHS intervention (N = 15) or control group (N = 15). Baseline measurements were conducted in August 2016 and the follow-up was conducted in May 2017. The intervention was designed to promote well-being (primary outcome) by focusing on physical activity, meals, sleep, sense of security, and stress (secondary outcomes). The intervention comprised: structural initiatives at the school level; a teaching material; peer-led innovation workshops; and a smartphone app. The 10-item Perceived Stress Scale was used to measure stress. Intervention effects on perceived stress were estimated using an intention-to-treat approach with multiple imputations of missing data and multilevel general linear regression modelling. A total of 4577 students answered the baseline questionnaire. No statistically significant difference was found in stress between students at intervention and control schools at the follow-up (mean score: 16.7 versus 16.7, adjusted b = 0.42, 95% CI: −0.16;1.00). The HHS Study is one of the first large randomized controlled trials targeting school environmental stressors. Potential implementation failures and the failures of the program theory are discussed.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bonnesen, Camilla Thørring","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Rod, Naja Hulvej","Toftager, Mette","Madsen, Katrine Rich","Jensen, Marie Pil","Rosing, Johanne Aviaja","Wehner, Stine Kjær","Due, Pernille","Krølner, Rikke"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735453"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Bonnesen, Camilla Thørring"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Denmark","Effectiveness","Exercise","Follow Up Studies","High school","Humans","School Health Services","School based intervention","Schools","Stress","Students"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preventing stress among high school students in denmark through the multicomponent healthy high school intervention the effectiveness at first follow up","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph20031754","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was funded by TrygFonden, grant number 30035 and Nordea-Fonden, grant number 02-2015-1364."],"id":"S02-100.00-735453","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9914335","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36767122","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85147822510","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-167adb41-3639-4e2e-93bc-dc1fc76d78fd","sdu-e5be9cce-9f3e-465f-bde5-7791b792957f"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Denmark","Exercise","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","School Health Services","Schools","Students","effectiveness","high school","school-based intervention","stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5A8E959FCD73854917E182B24FAA43A0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/391115828/ijerph_20_01754_v3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/222202219/ijerph_20_01754_v3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https: