ry":"dk","first":"Jens Laurids","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"365188dd-0cdc-4c71-a590-2ccd261ae3df","name":"Sørensen, Jens Laurids","orcid":"0000-0002-2392-5343","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens C.","key":"frisvadpau","last":"Frisvad","locid":"b2d4f948-9e1c-4f8c-9c02-05588bfa21b9","name":"Frisvad, Jens Christian","name_org":"Frisvad, Jens C.","orcid":"0000-0002-0573-4340","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Reinhard","key":"wimmerpau","last":"Wimmer","locid":"1d80e9f3-a391-40e6-a73a-84194aecbb6a","name":"Wimmer, Reinhard","orcid":"0000-0001-6942-5056","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Teis Esben","key":"sondergaardpau","last":"Sondergaard","locid":"c4550265-7489-4e7e-a723-b7cfef89912e","name":"Sondergaard, Teis Esben","orcid":"0000-0002-4455-7498","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fbr.2022.10.001","issn":["17494613","18780253"],"issn_org":["17494613"],"journal":"Fungal Biology Reviews","paperid":"100288","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fungal Biology Reviews","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141867707"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6f4bacaa-f933-42e1-88ce-1c732a6a77d4","dtu-748130ad-6ae9-4cd9-b6de-10f82d63b350"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Quick guide to secondary metabolites from <i>Apiospora</i> and <i>Arthrinium</i>","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.91-005393","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Some studies have found transportation noise to be associated with higher diabetes risk. This includes studies based on millions of participants, relying entirely on register-based confounder adjustment, which raises concern about residual lifestyle confounding. We aimed to investigate associations between noise and type 2 diabetes (T2D), including investigation of effects of increasing confounder adjustment for register-data and lifestyle. Methods: In a cohort of 286,151 participants randomly selected across Denmark in 2010–2013 and followed up until 2017, we identified 7574 incident T2D cases. Based on residential address-history for all participants linked with exposure assessment of high spatial resolution, we calculated 10-year time-weighted mean road and railway noise at the most (LdenMax) and least (LdenMin) exposed façades and air pollution (PM2.5). We used Cox models to calculate hazard ratios (HR) with increasing adjustment for individual- and area-level register-based sociodemographic covariates, self-reported lifestyle and air pollution. Results: We found that a 10 dB increase in 10-year mean road LdenMin was associated with HRs (95% CI) of 1.06 (1.02–1.10) after adjustment for age, sex and year, 1.08 (1.04–1.13) after further adjustment for register-based sociodemographic covariates, 1.07 (1.03–1.12) after further lifestyle adjustment (e.g. smoking, diet and alcohol) and 1.06 (1.02–1.11) after further PM2.5 adjustment. For road LdenMax, the corresponding HRs were 1.07 (1.04–1.10), 1.05 (1.02–1.08), 1.04 (1.01–1.07) and 1.03 (1.00–1.06). Railway noise was associated with HRs of 1.04 (0.98–1.11) for LdenMax and 1.02 (0.92–1.12) for LdenMin after adjustment for sociodemographic and lifestyle covariates and PM2.5. Conclusions: Long-term exposure to road traffic noise was associated with T2D, which together with previous literature indicates that T2D should be considered when calculating health impacts of noise. After sociodemographic adjustment, further lifestyle adjustment only changed HRs slightly, suggesting that large register-based studies with adjustment for key sociodemographic covariates can produce reliable results.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sørensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Frohn, Lise Marie","Khan, Jibran","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-681360"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Mette"],"keyword":["Lifestyle","Railway noise","Road traffic noise","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to transportation noise and risk of type 000000000002 diabetes a cohort study","src":["au","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85142732507","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Research described in this article was conducted under contract to the Health Effects Institute (HEI), an organization jointly funded by the United States Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) (Assistance Award No. R-82811201) and certain motor vehicle and engine manufacturers. The contents of this article do not necessarily reflect the views of HEI, or its sponsors, nor do they necessarily reflect the views and policies of the EPA or motor vehicle and engine manufacturers."],"id":"S03-100.00-681360","identifier":[{"id":"85142732507","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36402187","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-3d54a08c-b979-43ff-aac9-16a877dc8f01","ruc-7ce78a72-57d7-498f-87c3-9cca569eb7a0","sdu-e97ffc52-55ee-439c-9677-5f6b065f216b"],"keyword":["Lifestyle","Railway noise","Road traffic noise","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-AD0805014297422E9CDBA7C21F81F653"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Public health epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lau Caspar","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"1932f287-552d-4539-8153-b2fc204a703b","name":"Thygesen, Lau Caspar","orcid":"0000-0001-8375-5211","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Marie","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36402187"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2022.114795","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"journal":"Environmental Research","paperid":"114795","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"217"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142732507"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3d54a08c-b979-43ff-aac9-16a877dc8f01","ruc-7ce78a72-57d7-498f-87c3-9cca569eb7a0","sdu-e97ffc52-55ee-439c-9677-5f6b065f216b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-term exposure to transportation noise and risk of type 2 diabetes : A cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-681360","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background Social inequality in smoking remains an important public health issue. Upper secondary schools offering vocational education and training (VET) comprise more students from lower socioeconomic backgrounds and have higher smoking prevalence than general high schools. This study examined the effects of a school-based multi-component intervention on students’ smoking. Methods A cluster randomized controlled trial. Eligible participants were schools offering VET basic courses or preparatory basic education in Denmark, and their students. Schools were stratified by subject area and eight schools were randomly allocated to intervention (1,160 invited students; 844 analyzed) and six schools to control (1,093 invited students; 815 analyzed). The intervention program comprised smoke-free school hours, class-based activities, and access to smoking cessation support. The control group was encouraged to continue with normal practice. Primary outcomes were daily cigarette consumption and daily smoking status at student level. Secondary outcomes were determinants expected to impact smoking behavior. Outcomes were assessed in students at five-month follow-up. Analyses were by intention-to-treat and per protocol (i.e., whether the intervention was delivered as intended), adjusted for covariates measured at baseline. Moreover, subgroup analyses defined by school type, gender, age, and smoking status at baseline were performed. Multilevel regression models were used to account for the cluster design. Missing data were imputed using multiple imputations. Participants and the research team were not blinded to allocation. Results Intention-to-treat analyses showed no intervention effect on daily cigarette consumption and daily smoking. Pre-planned subgroup analyses showed statistically significant reduction in daily smoking among girls compared with their counterparts in the control group (OR = 0.39, 95% CI: 0.16, 0.98). Per-protocol analysis suggested that schools with full intervention had higher benefits compared with the control group (daily smoking: OR = 0.44, 95% CI: 0.19, 1.02), while no marked differences were seen among schools with partial intervention. Conclusion This study was among the first to test whether a complex, multicomponent intervention could reduce smoking in schools with high smoking risk. Results showed no overall effects. There is a great need to develop programs for this target group and it is important that they are fully implemented if an effect is to be achieved. Trial registration https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN16455577, date of registration 14/06/2018.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kjeld, Simone Gad","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Danielsen, Dina","Jakobsen, Gitte Sofie","Jensen, Marie Pil","Holmberg, Teresa","Bast, Lotus Sofie","Lund, Lisbeth","Pisinger, Charlotta","Andersen, Susan"],"cuid":["S02-099.60-044398"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kjeld, Simone Gad"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Cigarettes","Cluster randomized controlled trial","Educational Status","Female","Humans","ISSUES","Intervention","Schools","Smoking","Smoking epidemiology","Smoking prevention","Socioeconomic","Students","Vocational education","Vocational schools"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness of the multi component intervention focus on reducing smoking among students in the vocational education setting a cluster randomized controlled trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"http