86","name":"Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","name_org":"Søgaard, Ole S.","orcid":"0000-0001-9107-2023","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37696935"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41591-023-02547-6","issn":["10788956","1546170X"],"issn_org":["10788956"],"issue":"10","journal":"Nature Medicine","pages":"2547-2558","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Medicine","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170556818"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6ad91524-b672-49bf-9014-dbbc60094ffe","au-36275b18-109b-4217-a6fc-b06a25bf11c8","ku-9b764ba8-c4b8-4bab-8b84-751fea0ffc89","sdu-60122784-2e20-4387-bc8e-643b608821f5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of a TLR9 agonist and broadly neutralizing antibodies on HIV-1 persistence : the randomized phase 2a TITAN trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-715684","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Epidemiological studies reveal that marijuana increases the risk of cardiovascular disease (CVD); however, little is known about the mechanism. Δ 9-tetrahydrocannabinol (Δ 9-THC), the psychoactive component of marijuana, binds to cannabinoid receptor 1 (CB1/CNR1) in the vasculature and is implicated in CVD. A UK Biobank analysis found that cannabis was an risk factor for CVD. We found that marijuana smoking activated inflammatory cytokines implicated in CVD. In silico virtual screening identified genistein, a soybean isoflavone, as a putative CB1 antagonist. Human-induced pluripotent stem cell-derived endothelial cells were used to model Δ 9-THC-induced inflammation and oxidative stress via NF-κB signaling. Knockdown of the CB1 receptor with siRNA, CRISPR interference, and genistein attenuated the effects of Δ 9-THC. In mice, genistein blocked Δ 9-THC-induced endothelial dysfunction in wire myograph, reduced atherosclerotic plaque, and had minimal penetration of the central nervous system. Genistein is a CB1 antagonist that attenuates Δ 9-THC-induced atherosclerosis.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Wei, Tzu-Tang","Chandy, Mark","Nishiga, Masataka","Zhang, Angela","Kumar, Kaavya Krishna","Thomas, Dilip","Manhas, Amit","Rhee, Siyeon","Justesen, Johanne Marie","Chen, Ian Y","Wo, Hung-Ta","Khanamiri, Saereh","Yang, Johnson Y","Seidl, Frederick J.","Burns, Noah Z.","Liu, Chun","Sayed, Nazish","Shie, Jiun-Jie","Yeh, Chih-Fan","Yang, Kai-Chien","Lau, Edward","Lynch, Kara L","Rivas, Manuel","Kobilka, Brian K","Wu, Joseph C"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412807"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Taiwan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute of Analytical Chemistry and Food Chemistry","National Taiwan University Hospital, Taipei, Taiwan","Stanford University","University of Colorado School of Medicine","University of Southern California"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cannabinoid receptor 000000000001 antagonist genistein attenuates marijuana induced vascular inflammation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9400797/pdf/nihms-1820885.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-412807","identifier":[{"id":"35489334","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9400797","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85129930623","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000803014300008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-20816381-e100-4ec9-8d8e-652b3e5b13b9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4B815B3B71707AFAC57888CFAB8C0BCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9400797/pdf/nihms-1820885.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Grarup Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"institute of analytical chemistry and food chemistry