-1734","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Albert","key":"kolstadpau","last":"Kolstad","locid":"287e6e28-266e-42e8-aa6d-10dffb6dc51e","name":"Kolstad, Henrik A.","name_org":"Kolstad, Henrik Albert","orcid":"0000-0002-6535-4323","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34903140"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/07420528.2021.2010741","issn":["07420528","15256073"],"issn_org":["07420528"],"issue":"4","journal":"Chronobiology International","pages":"579-589","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Chronobiology International","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121445222"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","velux"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a6283f9b-8a06-4385-8c85-b2a006b1e439","au-c6c98f4a-60fc-412a-bfb5-25230296bd66","ku-836b4e55-fb87-47b4-9db0-921cfdb6bcae","nfa-1c9dd9c9-ddc3-49a8-b112-4eb31c922271"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"A longitudinal study of morning, evening, and night light intensities and nocturnal sleep quality in a working population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-766933","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Treatment with glucagon receptor antagonists (GRAs) reduces blood glucose but causes dyslipidemia and accumulation of fat in the liver. We investigated the acute and chronic effects of glucagon on lipid metabolism in mice. Methods: Chronic effects of glucagon receptor signaling on lipid metabolism were studied using oral lipid tolerance tests (OLTTs) in overnight fasted glucagon receptor knockout (Gcgr−/−) mice, and in C57Bl/6JRj mice treated with a glucagon receptor antibody (GCGR Ab) or a long-acting glucagon analogue (GCGA) for eight weeks. Following treatment, liver tissue was harvested for RNA-sequencing and triglyceride measurements. Acute effects were studied in C57Bl/6JRj mice treated with a GRA or GCGA 1 h or immediately before OLTTs, respectively. Direct effects of glucagon on hepatic lipolysis were studied using isolated perfused mouse liver preparations. To investigate potential effects of GCGA and GRA on gastric emptying, paracetamol was, in separate experiments, administered immediately before OLTTs. Results: Plasma triglyceride concentrations increased 2-fold in Gcgr−/− mice compared to their wild-type littermates during the OLTT (P = 0.001). Chronic treatment with GCGR Ab increased, whereas GCGA treatment decreased, plasma triglyceride concentrations during OLTTs (P < 0.05). Genes involved in lipid metabolism were upregulated upon GCGR Ab treatment while GCGA treatment had opposite effects. Acute GRA and GCGA treatment, respectively, increased (P = 0.02) and decreased (P = 0.003) plasma triglyceride concentrations during OLTTs. Glucagon stimulated hepatic lipolysis, evident by an increase in free fatty acid concentrations in the effluent from perfused mouse livers. In line with this, GCGR Ab treatment increased, while GCGA treatment decreased, liver triglyceride concentrations. The effects of glucagon appeared independent of changes in gastric emptying of paracetamol. Conclusions: Glucagon receptor signaling regulates triglyceride metabolism, both chronically and acutely, in mice. These data expand glucagon´s biological role and implicate that intact glucagon signaling is important for lipid metabolism. Glucagon agonism may have beneficial effects on hepatic and peripheral triglyceride metabolism.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Galsgaard, Katrine D.","Elmelund, Emilie","Johansen, Christian Dall","Billeschou, Anna","Kizilkaya, Hüsün Sheyma","Ceutz, Frederik","Hunt, Jenna Elizabeth","Kissow, Hannelouise","Winther-Sørensen, Marie","Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","Kruse, Thomas","Lau, Jesper F.","Rosenkilde, Mette M.","Ørskov, Cathrine","Christoffersen, Christina","Holst, Jens Juul","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488718"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cholesterol","Glucagon","Steatosis","Triglycerides"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glucagon receptor antagonism impairs and glucagon receptor agonism enhances triglycerides metabolism in mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molmet.2022.101639","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488718","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9706156","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000905344500003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85142673433","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36400402","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9f66c4b0-6226-426c-9f30-d5608b80bea5"],"keyword":["Cholesterol","Glucagon","Non-esterified/ free fatty acids","Steatosis","Triglycerides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-87E1AD1E02989AE9B0FB72C4E7353314"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/327934824/1_s2.0_S2212877822002083.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molmet.2022.101639","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Juul Holst Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine D.","key":"galsgaardpau","last":"Galsgaard","locid":"fd725ee8-8f2a-44c9-9e11-4db618356d5b","name":"Galsgaard, Katrine D.","orcid":"0000-0002-5679-2807","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emilie","key":"elmelundpau","last":"Elmelund","locid":"50e6c2dd-69fe-4d12-8038-b85e7de1816f","name":"Elmelund, Emilie","rank":2,"role