{"abstract":"Context The male hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal (HPG) axis is transiently active during the first months of life with surging serum concentrations of reproductive hormones. This period, termed minipuberty, appears to be essential for priming testicular function. Despite the central role for male reproductive function, longitudinal data on HPG axis activation in infancy is sparse. Objective To explore the dynamics of HPG hormone activity in healthy male infants, to assess the association of HPG axis activity and testicular volume, and to establish reference curves for serum levels of reproductive hormones. Design Prospective, longitudinal birth cohort (the COPENHAGEN Minipuberty Study, 2016-2018, 1-year follow-up). Setting Population-based. Patients or Other Participants Healthy, male, term, singleton newborns were followed from birth on with repeated clinical examinations including blood sampling during a 1-year follow-up. A total of 128 boys contributed to this study, while 119 participated in the postnatal follow-up. Main Outcome Measures Serum reproductive hormone concentrations and testicular volume. Results Reproductive hormone concentrations showed marked dynamics during the first 6 months of age. Gonadotropins, total testosterone, and insulin-like factor 3 peaked at around 1 month of age. Inhibin B, anti-Mullerian hormone, and testicular volume peaked at around 4 to 5 months. Correlations largely recapitulated typical HPG axis pathways but also differed significantly from adult men. Conclusions We demonstrate a temporal dissociation of Leydig and Sertoli cell activity during male minipuberty and provide reference curves for reproductive hormones.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Busch, Alexander Siegfried","Ljubicic, Marie Lindhardt","Upners, Emmie N.","Fischer, Margit Bistrup","Raket, Lars Lau","Frederiksen, Hanne","Albrethsen, Jakob","Johannsen, Trine Holm","Hagen, Casper P","Juul, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463025"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Anti Mullerian Hormone","BIRTH","BOYS","Cord blood","Infancy","Inhibin B","Male","Minipuberty","Reproduction","Sertoli","Serum","Testosterone","hypothalamic pituitary gonadal axis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic changes of reproductive hormones in male minipuberty temporal dissociation of leydig and sertoli cell activity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-463025","identifier":[{"id":"35225342","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000770115500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85130767485","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7460b30e-5b25-40ea-8e9d-576ece8f75dc"],"keyword":["ANDROGEN RECEPTOR EXPRESSION","ANTI-MULLERIAN HORMONE","BIRTH","BOYS","CORD BLOOD","INFANCY","INHIBIN-B","Leydig","SEMINIFEROUS TUBULES","SERUM","Sertoli","TESTOSTERONE","hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis","male","minipuberty","reproduction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61B3713ED1B6316B69FAE6CD0E8DF701"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alexander Siegfried","key":"buschpau","last":"Busch","name":"Busch, Alexander Siegfried","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marie Lindhardt","key":"ljubicicpau","last":"Ljubicic","locid":"444cb3c0-9c6f-4695-96db-9ff9baf23e46","name":"Ljubicic, Marie Lindhardt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Emmie N.","key":"upnerspau","last":"Upners","locid":"a9f0316a-169a-4e9d-8654-b060853c548e","name":"Upners, Emmie N.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Margit Bistrup","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"39ef465b-cef7-4017-886c-dc5b7c24f6ed","name":"Fischer, Margit Bistrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lars Lau","key":"raketpau","last":"Raket","name":"Raket, Lars Lau","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Hanne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob","key":"albrethsenpau","last":"Albrethsen","name":"Albrethsen, Jakob","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Trine Holm","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","name":"Johannsen, Trine Holm","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper P","key":"hagenpau","last":"Hagen","name":"Hagen, Casper P","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35225342"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgac115","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"1560-1568","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"107"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130767485"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7460b30e-5b25-40ea-8e9d-576ece8f75dc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dynamic Changes of Reproductive Hormones in Male Minipuberty : Temporal Dissociation of Leydig and Sertoli Cell Activity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463025","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Ethnography has much to offer research in social pharmacy and health services yet is rarely applied. This chapter provides an overview of the principles of ethnography starting with a brief historical account of the methodology. The first part of the chapter then explains how ethnography can shed light on the social context of pharmaceuticals, thereby introducing new ways of thinking, to researchers in the health and natural sciences. This is done by digging into the epistemology of ethnography, exploring how it differs from other methodologies (qualitative and quantitative), and how it builds on the core principles of constructivism and reflexivity. The second part of the chapter is concerned with how to conduct an ethnographic study, focusing on participant observation and fieldwork. Ethnography literally means “writing about people”; therefore, an entire section is devoted to various ways of writing up ethnographic data, from thick descriptions and field notes to social theory and analysis. Finally, there is a section on ethics, followed by advice on how to move forward with an ethnographic project. The chapter ends with some reflective questions and application exercises for designing an ethnographic study and training observation skills.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lau, Sofie Rosenlund","Kaae, Susanne","Kälvemark Sporrong, Sofia","Traulsen, Janine Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-502681"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the use of ethnography in social pharmacy and health services research","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-502681","identifier":[{"id":"85137576801","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b6ee31e7-bd85-4a4a-a0cd-ad3166f6f2f6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8F995D9D4C08CAFA851D6CE9D76F6EB5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sofie Rosenlund","key":"laupau","last":"Lau","locid":"a4b194c8-64b5-47a4-9c11-13fb48c7e884","name":"Lau, Sofie Rosenlund","orcid":"0000-0003-3377-4566","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne","key":"kaaepau","last":"Kaae","locid":"06ec1138-d761-4b0c-bafd-4433148f6fa2","name":"Kaae, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8187-365X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sofia","key":"kälvemarksporrongpau","last":"Kälvemark Sporrong","locid":"e3c3e35a-c010-4f3d-8f36-bc2c529e7de2","name":"Kälvemark Sporrong, Sofia","orcid":"0000-0001-5848-8625","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janine Marie","key":"traulsenpau","last":"Traulsen","locid":"85fbd5a2-c510-409f-bc5f-ef5d7d7eda15","name":"Traulsen, Janine Marie","orcid":"0000-0001-8927-4478","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/b978-0-323-91888-6.00034-x","edition":"1","eisbn":["9780323914260"],"pages":"329-344","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Contemporary Research Methods in Pharmacy and Health Services"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137576801"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b6ee31e7-bd85-4a4a-a0cd-ad3166f6f2f6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The use of ethnography in social pharmacy and health services research","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-502681","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) is a common disorder that requires more treatment options. Mobile health (mHealth) app interventions are promising for patients with PTSD, as they can provide easily accessible support, strategies, and information. However, knowledge about mHealth interventions is sparse and primarily based on quantitative studies. Objective: The aim of this study is to qualitatively explore the experiences of patients with PTSD with regard to using an mHealth app as a stand-alone intervention before commencing psychotherapeutic treatment. Methods: We conducted semistructured interviews with 14 participants 6 weeks after they received the app. The participants were all referred to PTSD treatment and were waiting to commence psychotherapeutic treatment. During this waiting time, the participants had no contact with the health staff. Interviews were transcribed and were analyzed using thematic analysis. Results: A total of 3 themes were identified—the use of app, being a patient, and the overall evaluation of the app. The use of the app was described with the subtheme of habits, and the theme of being a patient included the subthemes of having negative experiences with the app and being a part of a research project. The use of the app encompassed how psychological factors and technical problems could interfere with the use of the app. The theme of being a patient depicted that the waiting time before starting treatment was long, and a subgroup of patients experienced feeling worse during this time, which they partly attributed to using the app. Several suggestions for change have been described in the overall evaluation of the app. Conclusions: The findings in this study revealed that emotional arousal influenced the use of the app and that it was difficult for participants to establish a habit of using the app, thus reflecting the importance of supporting habit formation when implementing an mHealth app in mental health care services. This study makes an important contribution to the field of mHealth research, as it revealed that some participants had negative experiences resulting from using the app, thus reflecting the potential harm of having an mHealth app without the support of a clinician. It is therefore recommended to use a blended care treatment or an approach in which mental health care professionals prescribe an mHealth app for relevant patients to avoid increased suicidal risk.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Riisager, Lisa Grønberg","Christensen, Anne Bryde","Scharff, Frederik Bernt","Arendt, Ida-Marie T. P.","Ismail, Israa","Lau, Marianne Engelbrecht","Møller, Stine Bjerrum"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-595984"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Riisager, Lisa Grønberg"],"keyword":["App","Intervention","Mobile phone","PTSD","Patient experience","Posttraumatic stress disorder","Qualitative analysis","Smartphone","Thematic analysis","mHealth"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Psychotherapeutic Center Stolpegaard"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patients experiences of using a self help app for posttraumatic stress disorder qualitative study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/26852","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-595984","identifier":[{"id":"34346896","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8374664","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85112049858","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4f755cce-be37-4afb-808c-915c3199eb88"],"keyword":["App","Intervention","MHealth","Mobile phone","PTSD","Patient experience","Posttraumati