{"abstract":"Rapporten Sundhedstilstanden blandt personer med diabetes - Analyser baseret på Den Nationale Sundhedsprofil 2017 belyser sundhedstilstanden blandt personer med type 1-diabetesog type 2-diabetes inden for emnerne selvvurderet helbred og trivsel, sundhedsadfærd og overvægt, sygelighed og sygdomskonsekvenser og sociale relationer. Denne rapport benytter spørgeskemadata fra Den Nationale Sundhedsprofil 2017 og register-oplysninger fra Landspatientregisteret og Lægemiddelstatistikregisteret. Til at identificere personer med type 1- eller type 2-diabetes anvendes algoritmer baseret på oplysninger fra henholdsvis Landspatientregisteret og Lægemiddelstatistikregisteret, som benyttes i Register for Udvalgte Kroniske Sygdomme og Svære Psykiske Lidelser. For hver indikator foretages en sammenligning mellem personer med type 1-diabetesog type 2-diabetes og den øvrige danske befolkning.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Maja Bæksgaard","Lassen, Tina Harmer","Vulff, Helle Marie","Lau, Cathrine Juel","Davidsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-734131"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sundhedstilstanden blandt personer med diabetes analyser baseret på den nationale sundhedsprofil 000000002017","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/257119079/sundhedstilstanden_blandt_personer_med_diabetes_analyser_baseret_p_den_nationale_sundhedsprofil_201_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-734131","ids":["sdu-b4b4a7d2-7306-403e-97b5-5ef1e3462a54"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CFE24D661FB1E3ABD395129467DEDFDE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/257119079/sundhedstilstanden_blandt_personer_med_diabetes_analyser_baseret_p_den_nationale_sundhedsprofil_201_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sdu.dk/da/sif/rapporter/2020/sundhedstilstanden_blandt_personer_med_diabetes","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Bæksgaard","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"af767269-0170-462b-b796-d88cdff22809","name":"Jørgensen, Maja Bæksgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3465-0709","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina Harmer","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"f6b980ec-6ebd-4b2b-9075-1d3db3ad070c","name":"Lassen, Tina Harmer","orcid":"0009-0009-8724-510X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Marie","key":"vulffpau","last":"Vulff","locid":"98e54709-cb42-4c4f-b7d0-a9e2f300bc45","name":"Vulff, Helle Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine Juel","key":"laupau","last":"Lau","name":"Lau, Cathrine Juel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"cc8a107d-cac5-448c-b75f-3d80a7edbc95","name":"Davidsen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0001-6089-9781","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"89","publisher":"Syddansk Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b4b4a7d2-7306-403e-97b5-5ef1e3462a54"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sundhedstilstanden blandt personer med diabetes : Analyser baseret på Den Nationale Sundhedsprofil 2017","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-734131","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSETo provide evidence-based guidance on the clinical management of cancer cachexia in adult patients with advanced cancer.METHODSA systematic review of the literature collected evidence regarding nutritional, pharmacologic, and other interventions, such as exercise, for cancer cachexia. PubMed and the Cochrane Library were searched for randomized controlled trials (RCTs) and systematic reviews of RCTs published from 1966 through October 17, 2019. ASCO convened an Expert Panel to review the evidence and formulate recommendations.RESULTSThe review included 20 systematic reviews and 13 additional RCTs. Dietary counseling, with or without oral nutritional supplements, was reported to increase body weight in some trials, but evidence remains limited. Pharmacologic interventions associated with improvements in appetite and/or body weight include progesterone analogs and corticosteroids. The other evaluated interventions either had no benefit or insufficient evidence of benefit to draw conclusions on efficacy. Limitations of the evidence include high drop-out rates, consistent with advanced cancer, as well as variability across studies in outcomes of interest and methods for outcome assessment.RECOMMENDATIONSDietary counseling may be offered with the goals of providing patients and caregivers with advice for the management of cachexia. Enteral feeding tubes and parenteral nutrition should not be used routinely. In the absence of more robust evidence, no specific pharmacological intervention can be recommended as the standard of care; therefore, clinicians may choose not to prescribe medications specifically for the treatment of cancer cachexia. Nonetheless, when it is decided to trial a drug to improve appetite and/or improve weight gain, currently available pharmacologic interventions that may be used include progesterone analogs and short-term (weeks) corticosteroids.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Roeland, Eric J.","Bohlke, Kari","Baracos, Vickie E.","Bruera, Eduardo","del Fabbro, Egidio","Dixon, Suzanne","Fallon, Marie","Herrstedt, Jørn","Lau, Harold","Platek, Mary","Rugo, Hope S.","Schnipper, Hester H.","Smith, Thomas J.","Tan, Winston","Loprinzi, Charles L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-411328"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amer Soc Clin Oncol, American Society of Clinical Oncology","Cambia Hlth Solut","Dyouville Coll, D'Youville College","Harvard University","Johns Hopkins University","Mayo Clin, Mayo Clinic","University of Alberta","University of Calgary","University of California San Francisco","University of Edinburgh","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","Virginia Commonwealth University"],"keyword":["American Society","Body composition","CELL LUNG CANCER","Double blind","Parenteral Nutrition","Quality of Life","Randomized clinical trial","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"management of cancer cachexia asco guideline","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/275326280/Management_of_Cancer_Cachexia.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-411328","identifier":[{"id":"000559984900010","type":"wos"},{"id":"32432946","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088245439","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1e186275-4253-4dc2-82b1-46abafa9b9ff"],"keyword":["ADENOSINE 5'-TRIPHOSPHATE","AMERICAN SOCIETY","BODY-COMPOSITION","CELL LUNG-CANCER","DOUBLE-BLIND","MEGESTROL-ACETATE","PARENTERAL-NUTRITION","QUALITY-OF-LIFE","RANDOMIZED CLINICAL-TRIAL","WEIGHT-LOSS"],"lang":"English","l