{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Gillezeau, Christina","Ornstein, Katherine","Aldridge, Melissa","Gazibara, Tatjana","Groenvold, Mogens","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Kristensen, Marie Skov"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-605265"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new anti depressant utilization pre and post bereavement a population based study of partners and adult children","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-605265","ids":["sdu-700b0477-e3ae-46b0-b81f-a7cef05f49df"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-79A0466B4CB3C8688FD567662895FA4D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"gillezeaupau","last":"Gillezeau","name":"Gillezeau, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katherine","key":"ornsteinpau","last":"Ornstein","name":"Ornstein, Katherine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Melissa","key":"aldridgepau","last":"Aldridge","name":"Aldridge, Melissa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tatjana","key":"gazibarapau","last":"Gazibara","locid":"fb15e343-d5f6-4f13-b954-cace0cc3e8e5","name":"Gazibara, Tatjana","orcid":"0000-0002-9621-8375","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"groenvoldpau","last":"Groenvold","name":"Groenvold, Mogens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lau","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"1932f287-552d-4539-8153-b2fc204a703b","name":"Thygesen, Lau Caspar","name_org":"Thygesen, Lau","orcid":"0000-0001-8375-5211","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"ede804e9-f7b6-414e-a9bd-557cb33be5bb","name":"Kristensen, Marie Skov","name_org":"Kristensen, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-8066-8937","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-700b0477-e3ae-46b0-b81f-a7cef05f49df"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"New Anti-Depressant Utilization Pre and Post Bereavement: A Population Based Study of Partners and Adult Children","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-605265","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Patient-reported health-related quality of life is a complementary healthcare outcome and important when assessing treatment efficacy. Using COSMIN methodological recommendations, this study evaluates the validity and reliability of a core heart disease-specific health-related quality of life questionnaire, the HeartQoL questionnaire (Danish version) in a sample of patients following heart valve surgery. DESIGN: This project involved a cross-sectional validity study and a test-retest reliability study. METHODS: Eligible patients completed the HeartQoL, the SF-36 health survey questionnaire, and the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale following heart valve surgery. Construct validity was tested using a priori hypotheses. Internal consistency reliability was assessed with Cronbach's alpha. An independent sample of patients participated in the test-retest study and reproducibility was determined with relative [intra-class correlation coefficient (ICC)] and absolute reliability [standard error of measurement (SEM) and smallest detectable change (SDC)]. RESULTS: Internal consistency was high with Cronbach's alpha ≥ 0.87. ICC was 0.86-0.92. SEM ranged from 0.17 to 0.26 points and SDC ranged from 0.5 to 0.7 points. Construct validity was confirmed with 87% of all a priori hypotheses for predicted variables. CONCLUSIONS: The HeartQoL questionnaire demonstrates acceptable construct validity, internal consistency, and test-retest reproducibility in patients following heart valve surgery. Future studies should focus on assessing the responsiveness of the HeartQoL questionnaire over time and following heart valve surgery.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Grønset, Charlotte N","Thygesen, Lau C","Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","Zangger, Graziella","Kristensen, Marie S","Sibilitz, Kirstine L","Pedersen, Susanne S","Oldridge, Neil B","Zwisler, Ann-Dorthe"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-046620"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Wisconsin– Milwaukee"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cardiac Surgical Procedures psychology","Cross Sectional Studies","Denmark","Female","Health Surveys methods","Heart Valves surgery","Heart valve surgery","Humans","Male","Measurement properties","Middle Aged","Psychometrics methods","Quality of Life psychology","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measuring hrqol following heart valve surgery the heartqol questionnaire is a valid and reliable core heart disease instrument","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85059559337","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-046620","identifier":[{"id":"30610503","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85059559337","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d9bf7f33-5234-4c72-a99f-a7b53b7df49d","sdu-e1a97d4e-875f-40e3-acb4-d11761205e61"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cardiac Surgical Procedures/psychology","Cross-Sectional Studies","Denmark","Female","Health Surveys/methods","Health-related quality of life questionnaires","Heart Diseases/surgery","Heart Valves/surgery","Heart valve surgery","HeartQoL","Humans","Male","Measurement properties","Middle Aged","Psychometrics/methods","Quality of Life/psychology","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4AD56F3B82E41DA6FC243D843F2E3755"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of wisconsin milwaukee","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Wisconsin– Milwaukee","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte N","key":"grønsetpau","last":"Grønset","name":"Grønset, Charlotte N","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lau C","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"1932f287-552d-4539-8153-b2fc204a703b","name":"Thygesen, Lau Caspar","name_org":"Thygesen, Lau C","orcid":"0000-0001-8375-5211","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Selina Kikkenborg","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"92d15fb6-c29f-4d38-88a4-53d28ecc9a13","name":"Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graziella","key":"zanggerpau","last":"Zangger","locid":"4f4c0884-4346-4739-836f-e637c1922723","name":"Zangger, Graziella","orcid":"0000-0002-7606-3273","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie S","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"ede804e9-f7b6-414e-a9bd-557cb33be5bb","name":"Kristensen, Marie Skov","name_org":"Kristensen, Marie S","orcid":"0000-0002-8066-8937","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirstine L","key":"sibilitzpau","last":"Sibilitz","name":"Sibilitz, Kirstine L","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne S","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8ee710a4-b477-4b42-acf0-acf2bd8ddde2","name":"Pedersen, Susanne S.","name_org":"Pedersen, Susanne S","orcid":"0000-0001-8055-3251","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Neil B","key":"oldridgepau","last":"Oldridge","name":"Oldridge, Neil B","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Dorthe","key":"zwislerpau","last":"Zwisler","locid":"6e2c85c0-d456-45f2-a017-7942ea7eb12a","name":"Zwisler, Ann Dorthe Olsen","name_org":"Zwisler, Ann-Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0002-9241-2090","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30610503"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11136-018-02098-1","issn":["09629343"],"issue":"5","journal":"Quality of Life Research","pages":"1245-1253","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Quality of Life Research","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059559337"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d9bf7f33-5234-4c72-a99f-a7b53b7df49d","sdu-e1a97d4e-875f-40e3-acb4-d11761205e61"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Measuring HRQoL following heart valve surgery : the HeartQoL questionnaire is a valid and reliable core heart disease instrument","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-046620","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective This study examined the effectiveness of a workplace health literacy intervention on pain intensity, bothersomeness of pain, and sickness absence. Methods The quasi-experimental stepped-wedge cluster trial evaluated an intervention with two elements: (i) courses for employees and management to organize a joint foundation of knowledge about pain prevention and management with communication tools, and (ii) structured dialogs between employee and supervisor, to develop action plans to prevent and reduce pain. Monthly measurements were taken of pain intensity (0-10 scale), bothersomeness (days/month), and pain-related absence (days/month). Results Six workplaces were recruited, and 88% of employees (509) participated in evaluations. At baseline, mean pain level was 4.0, mean bothersomeness was 3.8 days/month, and mean pain-related absence was 0.6 days/month. From linear mixed models, pain intensity was reduced by -0.28 [95% confidence interval (CI) -0.52- -0.04] corresponding to a 7% reduction. For employees with pain >3 at baseline, the reduction was -0.74 (95% CI -1.11- -0.38) or 12%. There was no significant mean change in bothersomeness or sickness absence among all employees. Conclusion This intervention was both feasible and effective in shifting the overall mean pain level downwards for the entire population by 7%, with an accentuated effect among employees with pain levels >3. Organizing health literacy in nursing homes might be a feasible and effective way to build work environment efforts targeting the needs of employees. Future studies should investigate whether organizing health literacy is effective in other workplace settings and for employees with other health challenges.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Anne Konring","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Mortensen, Ole Steen","Punnett, Laura","Jørgensen, Marie Birk"],"cuid":["S03-099.65-768648"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cl