 Stefano","rank":56,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"22","corresponding":null,"first":"Jong-Hak","key":"woopau","last":"Woo","name":"Woo, Jong-Hak","rank":57,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sameen","key":"yunuspau","last":"Yunus","name":"Yunus, Sameen","rank":58,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3847/1538-4357/aaa298","issn":["0004637X","00670049"],"issn_org":["0004637X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Astrophysical Journal","paperid":"57","publisher":"American Astronomical Society","status":"p","title":"Astrophysical Journal","volume":"853"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041100305"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5d5d5e3b-7e49-4b21-8600-1cb3f9f620c6","ku-f99a44dd-ac6d-4eec-89a9-ade5d5a39e3c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gaia17biu/SN 2017egm in NGC 3191 : The Closest Hydrogen-poor Superluminous Supernova to Date Is in a \"Normal,\" Massive, Metal-rich Spiral Galaxy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-019450","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The aim of this study was to determine if hyperpolarized [1,4-13C2]malate imaging could measure cardiomyocyte necrosis after myocardial infarction (MI). BACKGROUND: MI is defined by an acute burst of cellular necrosis and the subsequent cascade of structural and functional adaptations. Quantifying necrosis in the clinic after MI remains challenging. Magnetic resonance-based detection of the conversion of hyperpolarized [1,4-13C2]fumarate to [1,4-13C2]malate, enabled by disrupted cell membrane integrity, has measured cellular necrosis in vivo in other tissue types. Our aim was to determine whether hyperpolarized [1,4-13C2]malate imaging could measure necrosis after MI. METHODS: Isolated perfused hearts were given hyperpolarized [1,4-13C2]fumarate at baseline, immediately after 20 min of ischemia, and after 45 min of reperfusion. Magnetic resonance spectroscopy measured conversion into [1,4-13C2]malate. Left ventricular function and energetics were monitored throughout the protocol, buffer samples were collected and hearts were preserved for further analyses. For in vivo studies, magnetic resonance spectroscopy and a novel spatial-spectral magnetic resonance imaging sequence were implemented to assess cardiomyocyte necrosis in rats, 1 day and 1 week after cryo-induced MI. RESULTS: In isolated hearts, [1,4-13C2]malate production became apparent after 45 min of reperfusion, and increased 2.7-fold compared with baseline. Expression of dicarboxylic acid transporter genes were negligible in healthy and reperfused hearts, and lactate dehydrogenase release and infarct size were significantly increased in reperfused hearts. Nonlinear regression revealed that [1,4-13C2]malate production was induced when adenosine triphosphate was depleted by >50%, below 5.3 mmol/l (R2 = 0.904). In vivo, the quantity of [1,4-13C2]malate visible increased 82-fold over controls 1 day after infarction, maintaining a 31-fold increase 7 days post-infarct. [1,4-13C2]Malate could be resolved using hyperpolarized magnetic resonance imaging in the infarct region one day after MI; [1,4-13C2]malate was not visible in control hearts. CONCLUSIONS: Malate production in the infarcted heart appears to provide a specific probe of necrosis acutely after MI, and for at least 1 week afterward. This technique could offer an alternative noninvasive method to measure cellular necrosis in heart disease, and warrants further investigation in patients.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Miller, Jack J","Lau, Angus Z","Nielsen, Per Mose","McMullen-Klein, Giles","Lewis, Andrew J","Jespersen, Nichlas Riise","Ball, Vicky","Gallagher, Ferdia A","Carr, Carolyn A","Laustsen, Christoffer","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Tyler, Damian J","Schrøder, Marie Krarup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228859"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperpolarized 000000000001 000000000004 000000000013c000000000002 fumarate enables magnetic resonance based imaging of myocardial necrosis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6231534/pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228859","identifier":[{"id":"29248653","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6231534","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85039066005","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ae79233a-0f91-44c4-86dd-3ec27acd1de0"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BB6FC8F2EAF940F5ADE17C1B41623660"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6231534/pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jack J","key":"millerpau","last":"Miller","name":"Miller, Jack J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Angus Z","key":"laupau","last":"Lau","name":"Lau, Angus Z","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Mose","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e1a60076-a622-4795-8777-6c13958aba7d","name":"Nielsen, Per Mose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giles","key":"mcmullenkleinpau","last":"McMullen-Klein","name":"McMullen-Klein, Giles","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew J","key":"lewispau","last":"Lewis","name":"Lewis, Andrew J","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nichlas Riise","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"dc7856f9-39e7-497a-a291-eab166abe2ef","name":"Jespersen, Nichlas Riise","orcid":"0000-0003-2502-2102","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vicky","key":"ballpau","last":"Ball","name":"Ball, Vicky","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ferdia A","key":"gallagherpau","last":"Gallagher","name":"Gallagher, Ferdia A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carolyn A","key":"carrpau","last":"Carr","name":"Carr, Carolyn A","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"ba5f7084-cbbb-4c1a-9fb6-85cce410d52a","name":"Laustsen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-0317-2911","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Damian J","key":"tylerpau","last":"Tyler","name":"Tyler, Damian J","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie A","key":"schroederpau","last":"Schroeder","locid":"fbaa0ecb-a7a6-49b7-bb10-96f34abac2f5","name":"Schrøder, Marie Krarup","name_org":"Schroeder, Marie A","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29248653"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcmg.2017.09.020","issn":["18767591","1936878X"],"issn_org":["1936878X"],"issue":"11","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"1594-1606","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039066005"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ae79233a-0f91-44c4-86dd-3ec27acd1de0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hyperpolarized [1,4-13C2]Fumarate Enables Magnetic Resonance-Based Imaging of Myocardial Necrosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228859","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Previous studies have demonstrated that using hyperpolarized [2-13C]pyruvate as a contrast agent can reveal 13C signals from metabolites associated with the tricarboxylic acid (TCA) cycle. However, the metabolites detectable from TCA cycle-mediated oxidation of [2-13C]pyruvate are the result of several metabolic steps. In the instance of the [5-13C]glutamate signal, the amplitude can be modulated by changes to the rates of pyruvate dehydrogenase (PDH) flux, TCA cycle flux and metabolite pool size. Also key is the malate–aspartate shuttle, which facilitates the transport of cytosolic reducing equivalents into the mitochondria for oxidation via the malate–α-ketoglutarate transporter, a process coupled to the exchange of cytosolic malate for mitochondrial α-ketoglutarate. In this study, we investigated the mechanism driving the observed changes to hyperpolarized [2-13C]pyruvate metabolism. Using hyperpolarized [1,2-13C]pyruvate with magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS) in the porcine heart with different workloads, it was possible to probe 13C–glutamate labeling relative to rates of cytosolic metabolism, PDH flux and TCA cycle turnover in a single experiment non-invasively. Via the [1-13C]pyruvate label, we observed more than a five-fold increase in the cytosolic conversion of pyruvate to [1-13C]lactate and [1-13C]alanine with higher workload. 13C–Bicarbonate production by PDH was increased by a factor of 2.2. Cardiac cine imaging measured a two-fold increase in cardiac output, which is known to couple to TCA cycle turnover. Via the [2-13C]pyruvate label, we observed that 13C–acetylcarnitine production increased 2.5-fold in proportion to the 13C–bicarbonate signal, whereas the 13C–glutamate metabolic flux remained constant on adrenergic activation. Thus, the 13C–glutamate signal relative to the amount of 13C–labeled acetyl-coenzyme A (acetyl-CoA) entering the TCA cycle was decreased by 40%. The data strongly suggest that NADH (reduced form of nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide) shuttling from the cytosol to the mitochondria via the malate–aspartate shuttle is limited on adrenergic activation. Changes in [5-13C]glutamate production from [2-13C]pyruvate may play an important future role in non-invasive myocardial assessment in patients with cardiovascular diseases, but careful interpretation of the results is required.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Chen, Albert P.","Lau, Angus Z.","Gu, Yi Ping","Schrøder, Marie Krarup","Barry, Jennifer","Cunningham, Charles H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-233737"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chen, Albert P."],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare","Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto"],"keyword":["DNP","Dobutamine","Heart","Malate Aspartate shuttle","Metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"probing the cardiac malate aspartate shuttle non invasively using hyperpolarized 000000000001 000000000002 sup 000000000013 sup c sub 000000000002 sub pyruvate","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85038388351","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-233737","identifier":[{"id":"85038388351","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29106770","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b6fb0aa2-7340-46f7-bfed-83c9d0c33d18"],"keyword":["13C MRS","DNP","Dobutamine","Heart","Malate-Aspartate shuttle","Metabolism","[1,2-13C]pyruvate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E02096E40F1EE50495397EC94553FD1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ge healthcare","name":"GE Healthcare","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"samuel lunenfeld research institute mount sinai hospital toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The MR Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Albert P.","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Albert P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Angus Z.","key":"laupau","last":"Lau","name":"Lau, Angus Z.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi Ping","key":"gupau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Yi Ping","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie A.","key":"schroederpau","last":"Schroeder","locid":"fbaa0ecb-a7a6-49b7-bb10-96f34abac2f5","name":"Schrøder, Marie Krarup","name_org":"Schroeder, Marie A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jennifer","key":"barrypau","last":"Barry","name":"Barry, Jennifer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charles H.","key":"cunninghampau","last":"Cunningham","name":"Cunningham, Charles H.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29106770"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nbm.3845","issn":["09523480","10991492"],"issn_org":["09523480"],"issue":"1","journal":"NMR in Biomedicine","paperid":"e3845","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"NMR in Biomedicine","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85038388351"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b6fb0aa2-7340-46f7-bfed-83c9d0c33d18"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Probing the cardiac malate–aspartate shuttle non-invasively using hyperpolarized [1,2-<sup>13</sup>C<sub>2</sub>]pyruvate","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-233737","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The parallel epidemics of childhood asthma and obesity over the past few decades have spurred research into obesity as a risk factor for asthma. However, little is known regarding the role of asthma in obesity incidence. We examined whether early-onset asthma and related phenotypes are associated with the risk of developing obesity in childhood.This study includes 21 130 children born from 1990 to 2008 in Denmark, France, Germany, Greece, Italy, The Netherlands, Spain, Sweden and the UK. We followed non-obese children at 3-4 years of age for incident obesity up to 8 years of age. Physician-diagnosed asthma, wheezing and allergic rhinitis were assessed up to 3-4 years of age.Children with physician-diagnosed asthma had a higher risk for incident obesity than those without asthma (adjusted hazard ratio (aHR) 1.66, 95% CI 1.18-2.33). Children with active asthma (wheeze in the last 12 months and physician-diagnosed asthma) exhibited a higher risk for obesity (aHR 1.98, 95% CI 1.31-3.00) than those without wheeze and asthma. Persistent wheezing was associated with increased risk for incident obesity compared to never wheezers (aHR 1.51, 95% CI 1.08-2.09).Early-onset asthma and wheezing may contribute to an increased risk of developing obesity in later childhood.","author_count":40,"contributors":["Contreras, Zuelma A.","Chen, Zhanghua","Roumeliotaki, Theano","Annesi-Maesano, Isabella","Baïz, Nour","von Berg, Andrea","Bergström, Anna","Crozier, Sarah","Duijts, Liesbeth","Ekström, Sandra","Eller, Esben","Fantini, Maria P.","Kjaer, Henrik Fomsgaard","Forastiere, Francesco","Gerhard, Beatrix","Gori, Davide","Harskamp-van Ginkel, Margreet W.","Heinrich, Joachim","Iñiguez, Carmen","Inskip, Hazel","Keil, Thomas","Kogevinas, Manolis","Lau, Susanne","Lehmann, Irina","Maier, Dieter","van Meel, Evelien R.","Mommers, Monique","Murcia, Mario","Porta, Daniela","Smit, Henriëtte A.","Standl, Marie","Stratakis, Nikos","Sunyer, Jordi","Thijs, Carel","Torrent, Maties","Vrijkotte, Tanja G.M.","Wijga, Alet H.","Berhane, Kiros","Gilliland, Frank","Chatzi, Leda"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-580613"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Biomax Informatics AG","CIBER Epidemiologia Y Salud Publica","CREAL","Centre for Infectious Disease Control","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Foundation for the Promotion of Health and Biomedical Research in the Valencian Region","French National Institute of Health","Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research – UFZ","Hospital del Mar","Institute of Human Genetics, Helmholtz Zentrum München","Karolinska Institute","Lazio Regional Health Service","Ludwig-Maximilian University of Munich","Maastricht University Medical Center+","Marien-Hospital Wesel","Pompeu Fabra University","University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust","University Medical Center Utrecht","University of Amsterdam","University of Bologna","University of Crete","University of Southampton","University of Southern California","University of Valencia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Stockholms Ians Landsting"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does early onset asthma increase childhood obesity risk a pooled analysis of 000000000016 european cohorts","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151773901/emss_82386.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-580613","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6