","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert D.","key":"gehrzpau","last":"Gehrz","name":"Gehrz, Robert D.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter A.","key":"milnepau","last":"Milne","name":"Milne, Peter A.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel A.","key":"perleypau","last":"Perley","locid":"55eafa9e-2eb9-4775-893e-830cd777d6a3","name":"Perley, D. A.","name_org":"Perley, Daniel A.","orcid":"0000-0001-8472-1996","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nathan","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Nathan","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Schuyler D.","key":"vandykpau","last":"Van Dyk","name":"Van Dyk, Schuyler D.","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3847/1538-4357/aacf8b","issn":["0004637X","00670049"],"issn_org":["0004637X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Astrophysical Journal","paperid":"20","status":"p","title":"Astrophysical Journal","volume":"863"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051470826"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e966c5e5-9258-4d39-9e02-e8e065ede1ba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SPIRITS 16tn in NGC 3556 : A Heavily Obscured and Low-luminosity Supernova at 8.8 Mpc","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532836","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background Patient-reported health-related quality of life is increasingly used as an outcome measure in clinical trials and as a performance measure to evaluate quality of care. The objective of this study was to assess the psychometric properties of the Danish HeartQoL questionnaire, a core heart disease-specific health-related quality of life questionnaire, in implantable cardioverter defibrillator recipients. Design This study involved cross-sectional and test-retest study designs. Method Implantable cardioverter defibrillator recipients in the cross-sectional study completed the HeartQoL, the Short-Form 36 Health Survey, and the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale. The HeartQoL structure, construct-related validity (convergent and discriminative) and reliability (internal consistency) were assessed. HeartQoL reproducibility (test-retest) was assessed in an independent sample of implantable cardioverter defibrillator recipients. Results Mokken scale analysis supported the bi-dimensional structure of HeartQoL among 358 implantable cardioverter defibrillator recipients. Convergent ( r > 0.72) and discriminative validity were confirmed. The HeartQoL scales demonstrated satisfactory internal consistency (Cronbach's alpha > 0.90). Test-retest reliability (two weeks interval) was assessed in 89 implantable cardioverter defibrillator recipients and found to be acceptable for each scale (intra-class correlation > 0.90). Conclusion The Danish HeartQoL questionnaire demonstrated satisfactory key psychometric attributes of validity and reliability in this implantable cardioverter defibrillator population. This study adds support for the HeartQoL as a core heart-specific health-related quality of life questionnaire in a broad group of patients with heart disease including implantable cardioverter defibrillator recipients.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zangger, Graziella","Zwisler, Ann-Dorthe","Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","Kristensen, Marie S","Grønset, Charlotte N","Uddin, Jamal","Pedersen, Susanne S","Oldridge, Neil B","Thygesen, Lau C"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-044487"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","OECD"],"country":["Bangladesh","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ibrahim Cardiac Hospital and Research Institute","University of Wisconsin– Milwaukee"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Arrhythmias Cardiac diagnosis","Cross Sectional Studies","Defibrillators Implantable","Denmark","Electric Countershock adverse effects","Female","Health Status","Humans","Implantable defibrillators","Male","Mental health","Middle Aged","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Psychometrics","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"psychometric properties of heartqol a core heart disease specific health related quality of life questionnaire in danish implantable cardioverter defibrillator recipients","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85040185710","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-044487","identifier":[{"id":"28952795","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85040185710","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-93f97675-70a6-4fcb-8c6c-e6829a31258e","sdu-db4c560d-7797-4d44-a3af-6922eeceb8d1"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Arrhythmias, Cardiac/diagnosis","Cross-Sectional Studies","Defibrillators, Implantable","Denmark","Electric Countershock/adverse effects","Female","Health Status","Humans","Implantable defibrillators","Male","Mental Health","Middle Aged","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Psychometrics","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult","surveys and questionnaires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8FD7AEB1F1C6F9C3D30241E65196D719"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, REHPA - The Danish Knowledge Centre for Rehabilitation and Palliative Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"bd","key":"ibrahim cardiac hospital and research institute","loc":["Bangladesh","Asia, South"],"name":"Ibrahim Cardiac Hospital and Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of wiscons