irst":"Nilanjan","key":"chatterjeenilanjanpau","last":"Chatterjee","name":"Chatterjee, Nilanjan","rank":350,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Laufey T.","key":"amundadottirlaufeytpau","last":"Amundadottir","name":"Amundadottir, Laufey T.","rank":351,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25027329"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/hmg/ddu363","issn":["09646906","14602083"],"issn_org":["09646906"],"issue":"24","journal":"Human Molecular Genetics","pages":"6616-6633","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Human Molecular Genetics","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938138638"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a3622933-558f-4536-8cce-2c99cc7b0156","nfa-a1fb962d-03e4-4fa1-bbfa-317cd0808cb7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Imputation and subset-based association analysis across different cancer types identifies multiple independent risk loci in the TERT-CLPTM1L region on chromosome 5p15.33","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.90-768382","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Preterm birth, low birth weight, and infant catch-up growth seem associated with an increased risk of respiratory diseases in later life, but individual studies showed conflicting results. OBJECTIVES: We performed an individual participant data meta-analysis for 147,252 children of 31 birth cohort studies to determine the associations of birth and infant growth characteristics with the risks of preschool wheezing (1-4 years) and school-age asthma (5-10 years). METHODS: First, we performed an adjusted 1-stage random-effect meta-analysis to assess the combined associations of gestational age, birth weight, and infant weight gain with childhood asthma. Second, we performed an adjusted 2-stage random-effect meta-analysis to assess the associations of preterm birth (gestational age <37 weeks) and low birth weight (<2500 g) with childhood asthma outcomes. RESULTS: Younger gestational age at birth and higher infant weight gain were independently associated with higher risks of preschool wheezing and school-age asthma (P < .05). The inverse associations of birth weight with childhood asthma were explained by gestational age at birth. Compared with term-born children with normal infant weight gain, we observed the highest risks of school-age asthma in children born preterm with high infant weight gain (odds ratio [OR], 4.47; 95% CI, 2.58-7.76). Preterm birth was positively associated with an increased risk of preschool wheezing (pooled odds ratio [pOR], 1.34; 95% CI, 1.25-1.43) and school-age asthma (pOR, 1.40; 95% CI, 1.18-1.67) independent of birth weight. Weaker effect estimates were observed for the associations of low birth weight adjusted for gestational age at birth with preschool wheezing (pOR, 1.10; 95% CI, 1.00-1.21) and school-age asthma (pOR, 1.13; 95% CI, 1.01-1.27). CONCLUSION: Younger gestational age at birth and higher infant weight gain were associated with childhood asthma outcomes. The associations of lower birth weight with childhood asthma were largely explained by gestational age at birth.","author_count":58,"contributors":["Sonnenschein-van der Voort, Agnes M M","Arends, Lidia R","de Jongste, Johan C","Annesi-Maesano, Isabella","Arshad, S Hasan","Barros, Henrique","Basterrechea, Mikel","Bisgaard, Hans","Chatzi, Leda","Corpeleijn, Eva","Correia, Sofia","Craig, Leone C","Devereux, Graham","Dogaru, Cristian","Dostal, Miroslav","Duchen, Karel","Eggesbø, Merete","van der Ent, C Kors","Fantini, Maria P","Forastiere, Francesco","Frey, Urs","Gehring, Ulrike","Gori, Davide","van der Gugten, Anne C","Hanke, Wojciech","Henderson, A John","Heude, Barbara","Iñiguez, Carmen","Inskip, Hazel M","Keil, Thomas","Kelleher, Cecily C","Kogevinas, Manolis","Kreiner-Møller, Eskil","Kuehni, Claudia E","Küpers, Leanne K","Lancz, Kinga","Larsen, Pernille Stemann","Lau, Susanne","Ludvigsson, Johnny","Mommers, Monique","Andersen, Anne-Marie Nybo","Palkovicova, Lubica","Pike, Katharine C","Pizzi, Costanza","Polanska, Kinga","Porta, Daniela","Richiardi, Lorenzo","Roberts, Graham","Schmidt, Anne","Sram, Radim J","Sunyer, Jordi","Thijs, Carel","Torrent, Maties","Viljoen, Karien","Wijga, Alet H","Vrijheid, Martine","Jaddoe, Vincent W V","Duijts, Liesbeth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-428898"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Ireland","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CIBER - Centro de Investigacion Biomedica en Red","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Department of Epidemiology, Lazio Regional Health Service","Erasmus University Rotterdam","Institut National de la Santé et de la Recherche Médicale (INSERM)","Linköping University","Maastricht University","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment","Nofer Institute of Occupational Medicine, Department of Environmental Epidemiology, Lodz, Poland.","Norwegian Institute of Public Health","Pompeu Fabra University","University College Dublin","University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust","University Medical Center Groeningen","University Medical Centre Utrecht","University of Aberdeen","University of Basel","University of Bern","University of Bologna","University of Bristol","University of Porto","University of Southampton","University of Turin","University of Valencia","University of Würzburg","Utrecht University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["David Hide Asthma and Allergy Research Centre, St Mary's Hospital, Newport, Isle of Wight, United Kingdom."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preterm birth infant weight gain and childhood asthma risk a meta analysis of 000000000147 000000000000 european children","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaci.2013.12.1082","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-428898","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4024198","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84899645523","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24529685","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3b6b10b8-c12a-4522-921e-af97a7576cb8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C05B8BBEEE0255AFCC53B040C50FCD4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaci.2013.12.1082","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"erasmus university rotterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Erasmus University Rotterdam","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"institut national de la santé et de la recherche 