","key":"salanpau","last":"Sala","name":"Sala, N.","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos A","key":"gonzálezcarlosapau","last":"González","name":"González, Carlos A","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"C. A.","key":"gonzalezcapau","last":"Gonzalez","name":"Gonzalez, C. A.","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23737080"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12263-013-0346-6","issn":["15558932","18653499"],"issn_org":["18653499"],"issue":"6","journal":"Genes & Nutrition","pages":"549-560","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Genes & Nutrition","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887237682"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6d15b8b3-4ee3-4f04-bb88-473443538d31","sdu-9a31ae8c-5707-4785-aef2-22cbe8706b04"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Vitamin C transporter gene (SLC23A1 and SLC23A2) polymorphisms, plasma vitamin C levels, and gastric cancer risk in the EPIC cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.74-020646","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"More than 40 genetic risk variants for type 2 diabetes have been validated. We aimed to test whether a genetic risk score associates with the incidence of type 2 diabetes and with 5-year changes in glycemic traits and whether the effects were modulated by changes in BMI and lifestyle. The Inter99 study population was genotyped for 46 variants, and a genetic risk score was constructed. During a median follow-up of 11 years, 327 of 5,850 individuals developed diabetes. Physical examinations and oral glucose tolerance tests were performed at baseline and after 5 years (n = 3,727). The risk of incident type 2 diabetes was increased with a hazard ratio of 1.06 (95% CI 1.03-1.08) per risk allele. While the population in general had improved glucose regulation during the 5-year follow-up period, each additional allele in the genetic risk score was associated with a relative increase in fasting, 30-min, and 120-min plasma glucose values and a relative decrease in measures of β-cell function over the 5-year period, whereas indices of insulin sensitivity were unaffected. The effect of the genetic risk score on 5-year changes in fasting plasma glucose was stronger in individuals who increased their BMI. In conclusion, a genetic risk score based on 46 variants associated strongly with incident type 2 diabetes and 5-year changes in plasma glucose and β-cell function. Individuals who gain weight may be more susceptible to the cumulative impact of type 2 diabetes risk variants on fasting plasma glucose.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Andersson, Ehm A","Allin, Kristine Højgaard","Sandholt, Camilla H","Borglykke, Anders","Lau, Cathrine J","Ribel-Madsen, Rasmus","Sparsø, Thomas","Justesen, Johanne Marie","Harder, Marie Neergaard","Jørgensen, Marit Eika","Jørgensen, Torben","Hansen, Torben","Pedersen, Oluf"],"cuid":["S03-090.38-007900"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Blood Glucose genetics","Body Mass Index","Denmark","Denmark epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 blood","Female","Follow Up Studies","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genetic Variation","Genome Wide Association Study","Genotype","Glucose Tolerance Test","Glycated Hemoglobin A genetics","Hemoglobin A Glycosylated","Humans","Incidence","Insulin Secreting Cells","Insulin Secreting Cells metabolism","Life Style","Male","Middle Aged","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Risk Factors","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["The Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Metabolics Genetics"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic risk score of 000000000046 type 000000000002 diabetes risk variants associates with changes in plasma glucose and estimates of pancreatic β cell function over 000000000005 years of follow up","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2337/db13-0362","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-090.38-007900","identifier":[{"id":"23835328","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84891500161","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3781471","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000324748200045","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-a3932e33-19a3-4dd8-a782-57027cd51e2c","ku-9baf7178-3d77-40e1-a56c-d515e16e30a7","sdu-0ab075f2-9f6d-45d6-83a6-c2d1db28c932"],"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Blood Glucose/genetics","Body Mass Index","Denmark","Denmark/epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/blood","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genetic Variation","Genome-Wide 